      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the expression \\(\\displaystyle\\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14}\\), we can use the difference of squares formula, which states that \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a + b)(a - b)\\). Here, \\(a = 235\\) and \\(b = 221\\). Applying the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n235^2 - 221^2 = (235 + 221)(235 - 221)\n\\]\n\nFirst, we calculate the individual sums and differences:\n\n\\[\n235 + 221 = 456\n\\]\n\\[\n235 - 221 = 14\n\\]\n\nNext, we multiply these results together:\n\n\\[\n456 \\times 14 = 456 \\times (10 + 4) = 456 \\times 10 + 456 \\times 4\n\\]\n\nCalculating each part separately:\n\n\\[\n456 \\times 10 = 4560\n\\]\n\\[\n456 \\times 4 = 1824\n\\]\n\nAdding these two results:\n\n\\[\n4560 + 1824 = 6384\n\\]\n\nNow, we divide this result by 14:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{6384}{14}\n\\]\n\nTo simplify \\(\\frac{6384}{14}\\), we perform the division:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{6384}{14} = 456\n\\]\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{456}\n\\]",
